      "summary": "Spread one ripple on the water, seen from straight above: outline-only rings in thin gray brush, stacked concentrically from the inside out around one point. The rings are not true circles: each differs a little in width and height, and the lines undulate, narrowly for the inner two and broadly from the third outward. Each outer ring is thinner, the fifth dashed and the sixth dotted as they break up. The written ring count (1–6), or 3–4 when none is written. The center is one of five positions around and slightly below the middle of the canvas."
